course: dictionary
lesson: 2547
title: Define: say exactly what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To define something means to say exactly what it means or what it is. When your teacher asks you to define a word, you give its meaning clearly, so anyone reading it knows exactly what you mean. «Can you define 'habitat'?» asks you to say, in your own words, what a habitat is.
explain: Define also works with rules and limits. «The rules define who can enter» means the rules say clearly who is allowed in and who is not. A definition shows the edges of a thing: what is inside it and what is outside it.
explain: You can also use define for shape and character. «a well-defined outline» is an outline with clear, sharp edges. «Kindness defines her» means kindness is the thing that most shows who she is. Whenever you meet define, ask: is it about a meaning, a limit, a shape, or the most important part of something?
fact: To define a word means to say exactly what it means.
fact: A definition is a clear, exact meaning, like one you would find in a dictionary or glossary.
fact: In maths we define shapes by their features: a square is defined as a shape with four equal sides and four right angles.
fact: «Don't let one mistake define you» means one mistake should not be the thing that describes who you are.
fact: In 1936 Turing described an imaginary machine that helped define what computers can and cannot do.
exercise: «Can you define 'habitat'?» What does define mean here? | To paint a picture of a habitat | *To say exactly what a word means | To run very fast | To count the animals in a habitat
exercise: «The rules define who can enter.» What does define mean in this sentence? | To shout the rules out loud | To forget the rules | *To state clearly who is allowed in | To break the door down
exercise: «a well-defined outline» What does well-defined tell you about the outline? | Coloured in with paint | Very large and heavy | Blurry and faint | *Clear and sharp at the edges
test: In maths, a square is defined as a shape with four equal sides and four right angles. What does define mean here? | *To say exactly what something is | To measure how heavy it is | To draw it very quickly | To hide it from view
test: Which meaning fits «Don't let one mistake define you»? | To be a tiny part of you | *To be the thing that shows who you are most | To write your name on the mistake | To stop someone from seeing you
exam: Which phrase uses define to mean to make the edges of something clear and sharp? | «Kindness defines her» | «The rules define who can enter» | *«a well-defined outline» | «Can you define 'habitat'?»
